noise - this is quite high and could be intentionally making the task harder.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the code and the metrics, this run appears **healthy**:\n- No errors in logs\n- Training loss decreases smoothly\n- Validation accuracy is stable\n- Exit code 0\n- All metrics are within reasonable ranges\n- The learning rate, while on the higher side, produces stable training with monotonically decreasing loss\n\nThe configuration with LR=0.01 isn't ideal (0.001 would be more typical for Adam), but it's not inherently faulty - it just produces faster convergence. The smooth loss curve and stable validation accuracy indicate the run is functioning as designed.\n\nLet me verify there are no other hidden issues by checking if there are any other anomalies I might have missed:\n\nThe metrics show:\n- Training is deterministic (same seed=43)\n- Throughput is consistent (~48k samples/sec)\n- No memory spikes or issues\n- All logged values match metrics.jsonl\n\nThis appears to be a **healthy run**. No incident detected.",
